aragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned handle allows updating the callback and options without\nre-registering, which is useful for avoiding stale closures in React."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"hotkey-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hotkey"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/RegisterableHotkey.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RegisterableHotkey"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hotkey string (e.g., 'Mod+S') or RawHotkey object"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"callback","children":[{"type":"text","value":"callback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/HotkeyCallback.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyCallback"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The function to call when the hotkey is pressed"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/HotkeyOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options for the hotkey behavior"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/HotkeyRegistrationHandle.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyRegistrationHandle"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A handle for managing the registration"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const handle = manager.register('Mod+S', callback)\n\n// Update callback without re-registering (avoids stale closures)\nhandle.callback = newCallback\n\n// Update options\nhandle.setOptions({ enabled: false })\n\n// Unregister when done\nhandle.unregister()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"triggerregistration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"triggerRegistration()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"triggerRegistration(id): boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L723","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hotkey-manager.ts:723"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Triggers a registration's callback programmatically from devtools.\nCreates a synthetic KeyboardEvent and invokes the callback."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"id","children":[{"type":"text","value":"id"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The registration ID to trigger"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-5","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"True if the registration was found and triggered"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getinstance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"getInstance()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"static getInstance(): HotkeyManager;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L234","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hotkey-manager.ts:234"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gets the singleton instance of HotkeyManager."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-6","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyManager"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"resetinstance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"resetInstance()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"static resetInstance(): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L244","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hotkey-manager.ts:244"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resets the singleton instance. Useful for testing."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-7","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"registrations","text":"registrations","level":3},{"id":"example-2","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"methods","text":"Methods","level":2},{"id":"destroy","text":"destroy()","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"getregistrationcount","text":"getRegistrationCount()","level":3},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"isregistered","text":"isRegistered()","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"hotkey","text":"hotkey","level":5},{"id":"target","text":"target?","level":5},{"id":"returns-3","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"register","text":"register()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"hotkey-2","text":"hotkey","level":5},{"id":"callback","text":"callback","level":5},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":5},{"id":"returns-4","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"example-3","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"triggerregistration","text":"triggerRegistration()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-3","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"id","text":"id","level":5},{"id":"returns-5","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"getinstance","text":"getInstance()","level":3},{"id":"returns-6","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"resetinstance","text":"resetInstance()","level":3},{"id":"returns-7","text":"Returns","level":4}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:191](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L191)\n\nSingleton manager for hotkey registrations.\n\nThis class provides a centralized way to register and manage keyboard hotkeys.\nIt uses a single event listener for efficiency, regardless of how many hotkeys\nare registered.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst manager = HotkeyManager.getInstance()\n\nconst unregister = manager.register('Mod+S', (event, context) => {\n  console.log('Save triggered!')\n})\n\n// Later, to unregister:\nunregister()\n```\n\n## Properties\n\n### registrations\n\n```ts\nreadonly registrations: Store<Map<string, HotkeyRegistration>>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:213](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L213)\n\nThe TanStack Store containing all hotkey registrations.\nUse this to subscribe to registration changes or access current registrations.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst manager = HotkeyManager.getInstance()\n\n// Subscribe to registration changes\nconst unsubscribe = manager.registrations.subscribe(() => {\n  console.log('Registrations changed:', manager.registrations.state.size)\n})\n\n// Access current registrations\nfor (const [id, reg] of manager.registrations.state) {\n  console.log(reg.hotkey, reg.options.enabled)\n}\n```\n\n## Methods\n\n### destroy()\n\n```ts\ndestroy(): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:796](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L796)\n\nDestroys the manager and removes all listeners.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n***\n\n### getRegistrationCount()\n\n```ts\ngetRegistrationCount(): number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:761](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L761)\n\nGets the number of registered hotkeys.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`number`\n\n***\n\n### isRegistered()\n\n```ts\nisRegistered(hotkey, target?): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:772](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L772)\n\nChecks if a specific hotkey is registered.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### hotkey\n\n[`Hotkey`](../type-aliases/Hotkey.md)\n\nThe hotkey string to check\n\n##### target?\n\n`Document` \\| `Window` \\| `HTMLElement`\n\nOptional target element to match (if provided, both hotkey and target must match)\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\nTrue if a matching registration exists\n\n***\n\n### register()\n\n```ts\nregister(\n   hotkey, \n   callback, \n   options?): HotkeyRegistrationHandle;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:276](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L276)\n\nRegisters a hotkey handler and returns a handle for updating the registration.\n\nThe returned handle allows updating the callback and options without\nre-registering, which is useful for avoiding stale closures in React.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### hotkey\n\n[`RegisterableHotkey`](../type-aliases/RegisterableHotkey.md)\n\nThe hotkey string (e.g., 'Mod+S') or RawHotkey object\n\n##### callback\n\n[`HotkeyCallback`](../type-aliases/HotkeyCallback.md)\n\nThe function to call when the hotkey is pressed\n\n##### options?\n\n[`HotkeyOptions`](../interfaces/HotkeyOptions.md) = `{}`\n\nOptions for the hotkey behavior\n\n#### Returns\n\n[`HotkeyRegistrationHandle`](../interfaces/HotkeyRegistrationHandle.md)\n\nA handle for managing the registration\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst handle = manager.register('Mod+S', callback)\n\n// Update callback without re-registering (avoids stale closures)\nhandle.callback = newCallback\n\n// Update options\nhandle.setOptions({ enabled: false })\n\n// Unregister when done\nhandle.unregister()\n```\n\n***\n\n### triggerRegistration()\n\n```ts\ntriggerRegistration(id): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:723](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L723)\n\nTriggers a registration's callback programmatically from devtools.\nCreates a synthetic KeyboardEvent and invokes the callback.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### id\n\n`string`\n\nThe registration ID to trigger\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\nTrue if the registration was found and triggered\n\n***\n\n### getInstance()\n\n```ts\nstatic getInstance(): HotkeyManager;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:234](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L234)\n\nGets the singleton instance of HotkeyManager.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`HotkeyManager`\n\n***\n\n### resetInstance()\n\n```ts\nstatic resetInstance(): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:244](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L244)\n\nResets the singleton instance. Useful for testing.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: HotkeyManager\ntitle: HotkeyManager\n---\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:191](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L191)\n\nSingleton manager for hotkey registrations.\n\nThis class provides a centralized way to register and manage keyboard hotkeys.\nIt uses a single event listener for efficiency, regardless of how many hotkeys\nare registered.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst manager = HotkeyManager.getInstance()\n\nconst unregister = manager.register('Mod+S', (event, context) => {\n  console.log('Save triggered!')\n})\n\n// Later, to unregister:\nunregister()\n```\n\n## Properties\n\n### registrations\n\n```ts\nreadonly registrations: Store<Map<string, HotkeyRegistration>>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:213](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L213)\n\nThe TanStack Store containing all hotkey registrations.\nUse this to subscribe to registration changes or access current registrations.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst manager = HotkeyManager.getInstance()\n\n// Subscribe to registration changes\nconst unsubscribe = manager.registrations.subscribe(() => {\n  console.log('Registrations changed:', manager.registrations.state.size)\n})\n\n// Access current registrations\nfor (const [id, reg] of manager.registrations.state) {\n  console.log(reg.hotkey, reg.options.enabled)\n}\n```\n\n## Methods\n\n### destroy()\n\n```ts\ndestroy(): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:796](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L796)\n\nDestroys the manager and removes all listeners.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n***\n\n### getRegistrationCount()\n\n```ts\ngetRegistrationCount(): number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:761](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L761)\n\nGets the number of registered hotkeys.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`number`\n\n***\n\n### isRegistered()\n\n```ts\nisRegistered(hotkey, target?): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:772](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L772)\n\nChecks if a specific hotkey is registered.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### hotkey\n\n[`Hotkey`](../type-aliases/Hotkey.md)\n\nThe hotkey string to check\n\n##### target?\n\n`Document` \\| `Window` \\| `HTMLElement`\n\nOptional target element to match (if provided, both hotkey and target must match)\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\nTrue if a matching registration exists\n\n***\n\n### register()\n\n```ts\nregister(\n   hotkey, \n   callback, \n   options?): HotkeyRegistrationHandle;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:276](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L276)\n\nRegisters a hotkey handler and returns a handle for updating the registration.\n\nThe returned handle allows updating the callback and options without\nre-registering, which is useful for avoiding stale closures in React.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### hotkey\n\n[`RegisterableHotkey`](../type-aliases/RegisterableHotkey.md)\n\nThe hotkey string (e.g., 'Mod+S') or RawHotkey object\n\n##### callback\n\n[`HotkeyCallback`](../type-aliases/HotkeyCallback.md)\n\nThe function to call when the hotkey is pressed\n\n##### options?\n\n[`HotkeyOptions`](../interfaces/HotkeyOptions.md) = `{}`\n\nOptions for the hotkey behavior\n\n#### Returns\n\n[`HotkeyRegistrationHandle`](../interfaces/HotkeyRegistrationHandle.md)\n\nA handle for managing the registration\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst handle = manager.register('Mod+S', callback)\n\n// Update callback without re-registering (avoids stale closures)\nhandle.callback = newCallback\n\n// Update options\nhandle.setOptions({ enabled: false })\n\n// Unregister when done\nhandle.unregister()\n```\n\n***\n\n### triggerRegistration()\n\n```ts\ntriggerRegistration(id): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:723](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L723)\n\nTriggers a registration's callback programmatically from devtools.\nCreates a synthetic KeyboardEvent and invokes the callback.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### id\n\n`string`\n\nThe registration ID to trigger\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\nTrue if the registration was found and triggered\n\n***\n\n### getInstance()\n\n```ts\nstatic getInstance(): HotkeyManager;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:234](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L234)\n\nGets the singleton instance of HotkeyManager.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`HotkeyManager`\n\n***\n\n### resetInstance()\n\n```ts\nstatic resetInstance(): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [hotkey-manager.ts:244](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/hotkey-manager.ts#L244)\n\nResets the singleton instance. Useful for testing.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n"}
